From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 15:44:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: enable EEE on MT7986 and MT7987

Only SoCs with the GMAC EEE capability get LPI interfaces, and only
MT7981 sets it. On MT7986 and MT7987, phylink therefore clears the
PHY EEE advertisement, and ethtool reports EEE as not supported. The
MediaTek SDK enables EEE on the GMAC of all these SoCs.

Set the capability on MT7986 and MT7987. Their PHYs keep the EEE
advertisement they have after reset, and userspace can enable LPI.
MT7988 stays without it, because all its PHY links use xGMII modes,
where the MAC has no LPI support.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.h |    4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.h
@@ -1239,13 +1239,13 @@ enum mkt_eth_capabilities {
 
 #define MT7986_CAPS  (MTK_GMAC1_SGMII | MTK_GMAC2_SGMII | \
 		      MTK_MUX_GMAC12_TO_GEPHY_SGMII | MTK_QDMA | \
-		      MTK_RSTCTRL_PPE1 | MTK_SRAM)
+		      MTK_RSTCTRL_PPE1 | MTK_SRAM | MTK_GMAC_EEE)
 
 #define MT7987_CAPS  (MTK_36BIT_DMA | MTK_GMAC1_SGMII | \
 		      MTK_GMAC2_2P5GPHY_V2 | MTK_GMAC2_SGMII | MTK_GMAC3_SGMII | \
 		      MTK_MUX_GMAC123_TO_GEPHY_SGMII | MTK_MUX_GMAC2_TO_2P5GPHY | \
 		      MTK_MUX_U3_GMAC23_TO_QPHY | MTK_U3_COPHY_V2 | \
-		      MTK_QDMA | MTK_RSTCTRL_PPE1)
+		      MTK_QDMA | MTK_RSTCTRL_PPE1 | MTK_GMAC_EEE)
 
 #define MT7988_CAPS  (MTK_36BIT_DMA | MTK_GDM1_ESW | MTK_GMAC1_SGMII | \
 		      MTK_GMAC2_2P5GPHY | MTK_GMAC2_SGMII | MTK_GMAC2_USXGMII | \
